Inputs use LF line endings, as git stores them; byte counts and hashes in this repository assume that.

## Performance

The converted compiler is slower than native Go. That is expected for a line-by-line translation running on a
different runtime, and it is improving. The table gives seconds. Each converted time is split into start-up (the
time before any TypeScript work begins) and work (everything after it), so the work column can be compared with
native Go directly.

